.TH WIZ3D-RUN 1 "October 2026" "wiz3d 0.3.1" "Sparky Stereo OS"
.SH NAME
wiz3d-run \- start a Direct3D 9 game with wiz3D stereo and declare its window to KWin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wiz3d-run
[\fB\-\-enable\-3d\fR | \fB\-\-disable\-3d\fR] [\fB\-\-steam\-app\-id\fR \fIID\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIargument\fR ...]
.br
.B wiz3d-run \-\-display\-settings
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs \fIcommand\fR with the d3d9 override for wiz3D and tells KWin, through
libstereo-declare, that the game's window holds full side by side, left eye first.
KWin chooses the output format in Display settings.
The wiz3D DLLs must be in the game's folder: copy
/usr/lib/wiz3d/x64 (64-bit game) or /usr/lib/wiz3d/x86 (32-bit game).
.PP
As a Steam launch option:
.B wiz3d-run \-\- %command%
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-3d
Declare the game window (default).
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-3d
Run the game without stereo and without a declaration for this launch.
.TP
.BI \-\-steam\-app\-id " ID"
Match steam_app_ID if Proton reparents the game (default: $SteamAppId).
.TP
.B \-\-display\-settings
Open Display settings (kcmshell6 kcm_kscreen).
.SH FILES
.TP
/usr/lib/wiz3d/x64, /usr/lib/wiz3d/x86
The Windows DLL trees to copy into a game's folder.
.TP
/usr/share/doc/wiz3d
Licences, notes and the record of what the build downloaded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The game's exit status; 1 if the game exits normally but no window was declared.
.SH AUTHOR
Sparky Stereo OS, an edition of SparkyLinux, created by Pawe\(sl "pavroo" Pijanowski and Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack).
